course: dictionary
lesson: 601
title: Awaken and awakened
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Awaken is a formal, story-like word that means wake up. Everyday talk usually says «wake up», but stories, poems and formal writing often use awaken. The forms awakens, awakened and awakening all come from the same word.
explain: Awaken can also mean that a feeling, memory or interest starts. «The trip awakened her love of nature.» Check by swapping in started: the trip started her love of nature. It still makes sense, so awakened means started here.
explain: In «His name means "the awakened one"», awakened describes someone who has come to understand something deeply. Buddhists see Siddhartha Gautama as a teacher who found a way to end suffering. A rude awakening is a different use: it means suddenly finding out something unpleasant.
fact: Awaken means to wake up, or to wake someone up.
fact: «Awakened» is the past form of awaken, and it is also used as an adjective.
fact: Awaken can mean to make a feeling, memory or interest start.
fact: «Buddha» means «the awakened one», and Buddhists generally see him as a teacher, not as a god.
fact: «A rude awakening» means suddenly finding out something unpleasant.
exercise: «Buddha» means «the awakened one». What does awakened mean here? | *Woken up and aware | Fast asleep | Very angry | Tired after a long walk
exercise: «The trip awakened her love of nature.» What does awakened mean here? | Put to sleep | *Made a feeling start | Made a loud noise | Ended for good
exercise: Animals awaken from hibernation in spring. What does awaken mean? | Go to sleep for the winter | Build a nest | Move far away | *Wake up after a long winter sleep
test: «A rude awakening» means what? | *Suddenly finding out something unpleasant | A happy surprise party | A rude word said at breakfast | A very loud alarm clock
test: Which everyday phrase means the same as awaken? | *Wake up | Doze off | Slumber | Yawn
exam: «The smell of baking awakened happy memories.» Which word could replace awakened? | Erased | Forgot | *Stirred | Hid
